bootstrap: app booted on a throwaway SQLITE db (234 libs)
rules: L1 user MM2 (any amount), L2 role BRANCH_MANAGER (>= 1,00,000)

=== A. rules configured, sender sends a DRAFT directly ===
    [MM -> SENT] warning: Marked sent and follow-ups scheduled; e-mail could not be sent now (check Settings → SMTP) — it has been logged.
      #1 Q-00001 r0 cur=1 SENT total=59000 contract=- steps=[]

=== A2. rules configured, approver uses direct APPROVED (routed into chain) / master override ===
    [MM -> APPROVED] warning: This quote needs multi-level approval for its amount / business unit — it has been submitted for approval (1 step(s)) rather than approved directly.
      #2 Q-00002 r0 cur=1 PENDING_APPROVAL total=59000 contract=- steps=["L1:user3:PENDING"]
    [ADMIN -> APPROVED] success: Quotation moved to Approved (ready to send).
      #3 Q-00003 r0 cur=1 APPROVED total=59000 contract=- steps=[]
      log: ["Approved directly by admin, bypassing the required approval chain (master override)."]

=== B. price raised 10x WHILE pending approval (chain was built for the old amount) ===
